{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"CONTEXT TAPE — Turn 47/314\n      \n        \n        \n          sys prompt\n          \n        \n        \n        \n          claude.md\n          \n        \n        \n        \n          Read t12\n          \n            \n          \n        \n        \n        \n          Bash t3\n          \n            \n          \n          STALE 44t\n        \n        \n        \n          Grep t5\n          \n            \n          \n          STALE 42t\n        \n        \n        \n          conv t45\n          \n            \n          \n        \n      \n      \n        ■ ACTIVE\n        □ STALE (no ref in 10+ turns)\n        ■ RECENT\n      \n    \n    \n      A — The Context Tape\n      Primary view: horizontal timeline of every block in the context window. Each bar shows a block's lifespan — when it entered, how big it is, and whether it's still being referenced. Stale blocks get dashed outlines and red highlights. Scrub through turns to watch blocks enter, age, and go stale.\n      \n        Strengths: Most visceral — you SEE the dead weight accumulating. Tells a story over time. Individual block tracking is front and center.\n        Weakness: Can get visually dense with 300+ turns and hundreds of blocks.","choice":"a","id":null,"timestamp":1780275718644}
